{
 "about": "Field classes of the food domain's types for the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D food). 'fields' classifies, for this domain's types (house_sim/data/types/food.json), every property of the type data the kernel's name table (watch_fields.json) does not, the food record's sub-keys (food.<key>: a domain entry for the head would hide the kernel's food.* rows, so every sub-key is listed, and food.* is the watched catch-all) and every field this domain's verbs, hooks and systems write on its types. identity = what a thing is (static props) and what the robot's processing made of a food (cut, peeled, parts removed, mixed, shaped, coated, seasoned); setting = a configuration the robot sets (a lid, a cereal liner, a sleeve still on, air pressed out); content = what it holds (food.qty_g, count, composition, volume_l: a portion taken out is a removal unless envelope.consume / deliver / consume_by names it); process = what heat and time drive (temperatures, ice, cook level, doneness, toast, ripeness, sogginess, proofing: food safety flags, invariants and the look-ahead cover them); condition = handling damage in its worse direction (bruised fruit, a cracked egg, torn dough, scorched or burnt food, split cream, shell bits or yolk fat in whites, a melted utensil); bookkeeping = records and mirrors (served_to, reported, made_on, derived_from, a vessel's food_contents) and a bulk portion's size_m, which follows its amount and its vessel. 'water_sensitive': paper packaging, the recipe card and the kitchen scale (house.wet). 'writes': names food writes on things of other domains' types (contamination, damage and soil keep the kernel's classes).",
